__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# The hooks are the instrument this repo measures with, so they ship -- as the
# TEMPLATE, which names no machine. The rendered `settings.json` carries this
# checkout's own venv path and is machine state, alongside settings.local.json,
# worktrees and the probe's own log. Tracking the rendered file is what deleted
# the Mac's four hooks on a pull (#125), because git overwrites an ignored file
# without a word. `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`, because git will not
# descend into an excluded directory and the negations below would never be
# read.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.template.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/probe-log.jsonl
.agent-yield/
